+2026-10-15 Bob implementation: install 48 reviewed unchanged Chinese original recordings across 18 cue groups; exclude row 34 and all generated samples. The user rejected v3 as incoherent; 17 adapted lines remain pending. The presentation-only director observes confirmed private views, distinguishes operator purchase tiers from equipment/spells, detects operator sales/promotions and available merges, and gives battle feedback on return to prep (first perfect defense, subsequent perfect defense, three-round streak or leaks). Only completed observed normal rounds qualify. New-game welcome is observed across the game-screen router; mounting/reconnecting does not replay history. Idle speech requires 20 quiet seconds, at least 15 remaining seconds (or untimed prep), no ready/pause/hidden state, once per round; first-round teaching is independently switchable. A bounded phase-local queue gives major events priority, waits for operator speech, cancels on phase change, mute, disable, hidden tab or unmount, and uses voice/master volume. Cue mapping and thresholds are explicit adaptations of the reviewed workbook, not claims about unpublished Hearthstone trigger code.
+
+2026-10-15 Bob frequency follow-up: routine purchase/sale/refresh/freeze/upgrade lines are probabilistic, with a shared seven-second cooldown, a 1.5-second attempt gap and four incidental lines per round. Rejected draws are not queued or retried. Major phase cues remain distinct. Exact probabilities are [ASSUMED] adaptation values, documented with sources and the approved-original installation procedure in docs/BOB.md.
+
+2026-10-15 final voice policy (explicit user confirmation): use original Chinese wording and recordings only. Retain the 65 enabled / 15 excluded script decisions and row 34 exclusion. Restore all adapted wording to the corresponding original, including Hearthstone names and minion terminology. 60 enabled recordings are installed; original files for rows 2, 6, 7, 36, 44 are unavailable locally and remain unplayed. No AI sample is enabled; generated lines and model fine-tuning are no longer pending release work. Existing probabilities, cooldowns, phase mapping and squelch behavior remain. Strategy-selection recording joins its existing strategy cue.
+
+2026-10-15 original-audio recovery: a full scan of 413 local zhCN audio bundles recovered rows 2, 6 and 44 under AudioClip IDs without the old a/b suffix. Original WAVs and transcripts match the reviewed lines; generation-plan audioId records the explicit aliases. The installer preserves script IDs and reads the actual audioId. 63 originals now play; rows 7 and 36 remain unavailable in the scanned client. Row 34 remains excluded. No synthetic or unrelated replacement audio.
+
+Bob portrait anchoring fix (2026-10-15): speech captions are absolutely positioned below the avatar and no longer contribute to the fixed wrapper width. The avatar retains identical bounds before/during speech; the caption stays within desktop and narrow viewports. Audio events and probabilities are unchanged.
+
+2026-10-15 spell drop follow-up: remove the standalone Amiya assistant; global spells accept any normal battlefield cell, including occupied and non-deployable cells. Targeted spells require an operator; Support still requires empty ground. Spell descriptions remain unchanged.
+
+2026-10-15 Bob frequency tuning [ASSUMED]: no per-round total cap. Routine cues share 8 seconds; refresh has 20 seconds between played lines and 10% chance. Failed rolls may retry on subsequent actions after the 3-second attempt gap. Purchase chance 20%; see BOB.md for other categories.
+
+2026-10-15 phase narration: welcome, prep, combat and prep battle-outcome cues bypass playback and attempt cooldowns; their existing probabilities remain unchanged. An accepted new queued cue immediately cancels the current narrator and caption. Operator voice priority and mute remain respected.
+
+Community compatibility preview: sp-mp 1.2.1 provides 4/8/12-seat rooms with population-scaled pools; room capacity is independent of tavern spells/heroes. Independent chat-bubble and dmg-board packages use a narrowly scoped adapter; local switches unmount their panels. Chat transport validates room membership and server-owned identity, limits input and rate; it never changes gameplay. See [community compatibility](../COMMUNITY-COMPAT.md).
